### B. Advance Repayable Calculation Engine
Implemented in [`VacateRequestService.java`](file:///C:/Users/Biju%20K/Desktop/rum/rms-backend/src/main/java/com/rms/backend/vacate/service/VacateRequestService.java):
1. **Notice Days**: Difference between `requestDate` and `expectedLeavingDate`.
2. **Repayment Formula**:
   - If $\text{Notice Days} \ge 30$: Full refund of advance paid:
     $$\text{Repayable} = \text{advance\_paid} - (\text{maintenance} + \text{breakage})$$
   - If $\text{Notice Days} < 30$: Pro-rated refund:
     $$\text{Repayable} = \left(\frac{\text{advance\_paid}}{30.0} \times \text{Notice Days}\right) - (\text{maintenance} + \text{breakage})$$
   - Guaranteed non-negative ($\ge \text{₹}0$).
3. **Live Placeholder**: Displayed to the tenant on the external form and to the property manager during notice review.

*User Specification Example Tested & Verified:*
- Advance Paid: ₹12,000
- Request Date: 05.09.2026 | Leaving Date: 25.09.2026 (20 days notice)
- Formula: $(12,000 / 30) \times 20 = \text{₹}8,000.00$ refund.

